CHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block C   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm portion of breast tissue which is oriented by the surgeon with a long suture designating  lateral  and a short suture designating  superior   There is an ill defined  tan yellow indurated irregular area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  Dispersed within this area are three tan gritty  ill defined foci measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial as follows  A  Lateral margin en face  B  Suspicious focus to posterior margin  C D  Suspicious focus to inferior margin  E  Ill defined lobular area to anterior margin  F  Suspicious focus to superior margin  G H  Suspicious focus to posterior margin  I  Grossly unremarkable to superior margin  J  Medial margin en face  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  medial half of cavity  are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm of irregular  unoriented portions of tan yellow to pink lobulated fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable tan yellow to pink cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes K T  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral half of cavity  are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm of unoriented  irregular tan yellow to pink lobulated portions of fibroadipose tissue  The specimens are serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable tan yellow to pink cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes U Z  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm irregular  tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple tan pink rubbery lymph nodes ranging from 0 3cm to 1 8cm in maximum dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassettes AA DD with three whole lymph nodes in AA  one bisected node in BB  two whole lymph nodes in CC and five whole lymph node in DD  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular  tan yellow to pink  unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue containing three tan pink possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 7cm in maximum dimension  The three possible lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassette EE  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  MJF                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST LEFT MEDIAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY  EXCISION PART C  BREAST LEFT LATERAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY  EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART E  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLA ADDITIONAL  EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 46 CLINICAL DATA    breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   INCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  MOST CONSISTENT WITH DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 OF 3  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Because of an appearance that is not typical for breast carcinoma  immunoperoxidase stains are performed to better characterize the cell lineage  The tumor cells are positive diffusely for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID protein and focally for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   cytokeratin 7 and vimentin  but are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   cytokeratin 20 and thyroglobulin  These findings are most consistent with a primary breast carcinoma  exclude a thyroid origin  and do not support a pulmonary or intestinal origin  BONE  RIGHT FEMUR  SUBTROCHANTERIC   BIOPSY  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  BONE  RIGHT FEMUR  SUBTROCHANTERIC   BIOPSY  FRAGMENTS OF BONE AND MARROW  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 19 04                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block D   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 10 43 Proofread by  Carole Fleming  Autopsy Secretary GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right femur subtrochanteric lesion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of tan red soft tissue admixed with bone fragments in which the soft tissue is entirely frozen as FX 1  now as A  The bone fragments are submitted in toto as B  after decalcification  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of tan red irregular soft tissue in which a representative is frozen as FX 2  now as C  The remainder of the specimen is entirely submitted as D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right femur intratrochanteric lesion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate of tan irregular soft tissue which is submitted in toto as E  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  AER      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BONE  RIGHT FEMUR SUBTROCHANTERIC   METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  O R  Resident  AQING   AHCHEAN   CHEN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  LAN WANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ajeya P Joshi  M D  PART A  BONE  RIGHT FEMUR  SUBTROCHANTERIC   BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY PART C  BONE  RIGHT FEMUR  INTRATROCHANTERIC   BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 AUG 99 ACCESSIONED ON  13 AUG 99 at 15 04 CLINICAL DATA  Known left breast cancer  Reviewed at Brigham and Women s Hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Grade  2  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Positive along a broad front at the medial margin of the specimen  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 2cm from the anterior superolateral margin of the specimen along a broad front  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within the region of the mass  Stains for receptors  Requested  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR MEDIAL   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  THREE FOCI  EACH REMOVED_DATE CM WITH A FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  PRESENT AT INKED SURFACES  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR MEDIAL   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEVERAL FOCI   THE LARGEST OF WHICH IS REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT INKED SURFACES AND WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEVERAL FOCI  THE LARGEST OF WHICH IS REMOVED_DATE CM  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  1  see note   Number of lymph nodes examined  1  Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  1 lymph node with scattered microscopic foci  Size of largest lymph node  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  NOTE  A single microscopic cluster of atypical cells is present in the frozen section and  retrospectively represent a single micrometastasis  Diagnosis by  STEPHEN LAU  MD Signed On  18 AUG 99 at 18 09 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 AUG 99 at 08 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Laboratory  labelled with the patient s name  number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 4cm  tan yellow  soft fragment of tissue  frozen entirely as FX  1 and resubmitted in A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is an 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm lumpectomy specimen with a localizing wire and long and short sutures demarcating the lateral and superior aspects respectively  The specimen is received partly bisected from lateral to medial and sutured by the surgeon so that only the true margins are exposed  The specimen is inked entirely in black with the lateral aspect overinked blue  the anterior margin overinked yellow and the inferior aspect overinked red  The specimen is sectioned to reveal multiple tan  firm nodular areas with adjacent granular less firm regions altogether measuring 7 x 4 x 2cm  The nodular areas extends to 0 2cm from the lateral  inferior  and lateral superior aspects of the specimen  and the granular less firm areas grossly abuts the medial margin  SECTION CODE  B  representative section of firm nodular area with closest anterior superolateral margin  C  representative section of firm nodular area with closest anterior superior margin  from medial aspect of specimen  D  representative section of firm nodular area with closest lateral inferior margin  E  lateral margin  F  medial margin  G  additional representative section of tumor  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  skin  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm skin ellipse excised to a depth of 0 5cm  The specimen is inked  bissected and submitted entirely in H I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior medial left breast  are two fragments of irregularly shaped  firm  fibrofatty tissue  the larger measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and the smaller fragment masuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Both fragments are inked entirely in black and serially sectioned to reveal a yellow cut surface  The specimens are submitted in their entirety in cassettes J through N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior medial left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregularly shaped  firm piece of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked entirely in black and serially sectioned to reveal a white yellow cut surface with focal red brown areas  The specimen is submitted entirely in O and P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior lateral margin left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm irregularly shaped  firm  piece of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked entirely in black and serially sectioned to reveal a green white cut surface with focal red brown areas  In two of the cut sections  a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm cyst is present that extends to 0 1cm from the inked margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes Q through S  Gross Description by  AARON CAPLAN  MD Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LYMPH NODE  L AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   INVASIVE CARCINOMA PRESENT AT REMOVED_DATE TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERFICIAL LATERAL MARGIN WITH SUSPICIOUS CHANGES AT THE MEDIAL MARGIN  O R  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   EXCISIO PART B  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR MEDIAL   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR MEDIAL   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 42 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT   LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  ATROPHY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  Medial    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled  lateral right breast  are two portions of breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Both are inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable parenchyma  No discrete lesions are noted  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through C  Labeled  medial right breast  are two portions of breast tissue  1 x 1 x 1cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Both are inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm firm area abutting the inked resection margin grossly  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in cassette D  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes E through H  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   MEDIAL RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA VERY CLOSE TO OR AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MEDIAL    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
