Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 AUG 93 ACCESSIONED ON  31 AUG 93 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA  Right mastectomy in a 42 year old female  Status post microcalcifications on mammogram and a breast biopsy with needle localization which showed infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED AND EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO AND SOLID TYPE  THE MARGINS OF RESECTION ARE NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE  NOTE  A residual 0 7cm infiltrating ductal carcinoma is present adjacent to the site of previous biopsy  In addition  a second focus of infiltrating ductal carcinoma  2 3cm   is present 4cm from the biopsy cavity and is arising in a background of extensive intraductal carcinoma  2  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 3 OF 21 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Macroscopic tumor nearly completely replaces one node but does not extend beyond the capsule  the other two nodes contain microscopic metastases  3  SKIN  SCAR AND FOREIGN BODY REACTION  NIPPLE  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 19 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 33     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is 365 gram  19 x 14 x 1 8cm mastectomy specimen  On the superficial surface  there is a 17 x 6 skin elipse containing a 1 3cm grossly unremarkable nipple and a 3 5cm well healed linear scar  3cm