Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 06 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG THE BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SCANT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The appearance of this tumor differs somewhat from the appearance of the tumor resected from the patient s right breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 0cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan yellow circumscribed firm nodule that abuts the inked margin  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in cassette A  The nodule is submitted in cassettes B through D  and the remaining tissue in cassettes E through G  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA PRESENT AT THE INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
