Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE RESECTION MARGIN  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  PRESENT AT MEDIAL INKED MARGINS  AND WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF ANTERIOR SUPERIOR MARGINS  HEALING PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE  BREAST  SUPERIOR  ADDITIONAL MARGINS    EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING THROUGH THE SPECIMEN TO THE NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN AT MULTIPLE SITES  BREAST  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS   SINGLE FOCUS OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU PRESENT AT THE TISSUE EDGE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 24 OF 24 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five specimens  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right breast lump  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm oriented breast specimen  The superior half is inked in black  inferior half in blue and the anterior half is overinked in green  It is sectioned to reveal a white to gray  stellate area measuring 0 8cm in greatest dimension and 0 4cm from the superior  closest  resection margin in the lateral half of the specimen  This area is submitted entirely in cassettes A through C with additional sections of the lateral half in D through F  Representative sections of the medial half are submitted in G and H  Labeled  additional superior margin  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating the superior aspect which is inked in black while the opposite inferior aspect is inked in blue  and a long stitch designating lateral aspect  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  representative sections are submitted lateral to medial in cassettes I through M  Labeled  final shaved margins  right breast  are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm in aggregate  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  entirely submitted in cassettes N through R  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm in greatest dimension tan pink area which may represent a lymph node  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette S  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes T through Z  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   RESIDUAL CARCINOMA PRESENT  MARGINS GROSSLY NEGATIVE  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  SUPERIOR  ADDITIONAL MARGINS   PART C  BREAST  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS  PART D  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  PART E  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY CONTENTS    report_end  , Unchecked.
