ription error in the note specifying the block containing the intravascular epithelium  The diagnoses remain unchanged  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  sentinel node  left axilla  hot and blue   691   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink soft tissue with one candidate lymph node  The specimen is bisected and frozen entirely as FX  1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm left simple mastectomy with a short suture designating the superior aspect and a long suture designating the lateral aspect  The anterior is inked blue and the posterior inked black  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal multiple cysts measuring up to 1 1cm in diameter  filled with clear to somewhat thick and tan fluid  There is a red tan linear area which may represent a previous biopsy site measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  at approximately the 12 o clock position  1 2cm from the anterior margin  and 2 1cm from the posterior margin  In addition  there are several hemorrhagic areas  mainly in the upper inner and upper outer quadrants  No discrete mass lesions are identified  The upper outer quadrant breast tissue is palpated for lymph nodes  and no lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  from medial to lateral  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant at approximately 11 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant tissue from approximately 7 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area at approximately 12 o clock  just under nipple  demonstrating cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic area at approximately 12 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic area just under nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible biopsy site at 12 o clock to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of biopsy site to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mid outer breast tissue from approximately 2 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic area in upper outer quadrant at approximately 1 o clock to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer tissue from approximately 4 o clock to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of hemorrhagic area under nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Small nodular fibrous area in upper outer quadrant  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  1 by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additi