aining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a 110 gram resection specimen of breast tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with contiguous axillary tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm with a long suture designating a breast mass and short suture designating the lower cephalad margin of the axillary tissue  The external surface of the breast tissue and axillary contents is lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Within the breast tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm mobile well circumbscribed nodule 1 5cm  from the superior aspect and within 0 2cm  of the anterior and deep margins  The external surface is inked black with the posterior aspect inked yellow on black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a well circumscribed pink tan mass REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm in greatest dimension extending to within 0 5cm of the anterior resection margin and to within less than 0 1cm of the deep margin  The remaining tissue is strands of white pink rubbery breast parenchyma within lobulated yellow adipose tissue  Within the axilla are multiple large firm lymph nodes which on cross section have a white tan appearance  these range in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The largest three are bisected and submitted in cassettes A and B  Remaining lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassette C  Section code A C Ax