or progesterone receptor protein with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 33     ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum           ELECTRON MICROSCOPY    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        RIGHT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH A FOCAL NEUROENDOCRINE COMPONENT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Groups of neoplastic cells containing dense core type granules are found focally within the specimen  Elsewhere  the cells are typical for ductal carcinoma of the breast  showing numerous intracytoplasmic lumens  Approximately 5  of breast carcinomas show focal neuroendocrine cells  and the prognosis is reportedly unaffected  1   Reference   1   Scopsi L  et al  Amer J  Surg  Path 16 561 576   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Added by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  9 o clock lateral right breast   is a discoid piece of pink yellow soft tissue  2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Sectioning reveals an irregularly shaped  0 6cm in diameter  white nodule  Submitted entirely in AA and BB  Received fresh in the frozen section lab in two separately labeled parts  Labeled  A   right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of breast tissue with a suture at the deepest resection margin  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm red tan firm nodular area extending to within 0 2cm from inked resection margin  Representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  A B  remaining non frozen nodule  C  deepest resecti