Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 20 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer with positive margin  Per PCIS  invasive cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT MEDIAL ASPECT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL ASPECT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 49                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  medial aspect   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast that is oriented by the surgeon with the single long stitch superior  the single short stitch lateral  and the double short stitch anterior  surface furthest from the tumor   The specimen is inked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  superior edge overinked orange  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly fibroadipose tissue  with a focal  ill  defined  tan white fibrous and hemorrhagic area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm that extends to the deep margin and to 0 3cm of the anterior margin  surfaced furthest away from tumor   This area  consistent with biopsy cavity  is entirely submitted in A D  with representative sections of breast away from the biopsy cavity in E and F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  B  right breast  lateral aspect   are 3 pieces of breast  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Each piece is unoriented and inked entirely in black  The largest piece is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly yellow gold adipose tissue  with a focal tan pink area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The specimen is entirely submitted in G J  with the focally tan pink portion in I  The medium sized piece is really sectioned to reveal predominantly yellow gold adipose tissue with a focal area of tan white fibrosis admixed with hemorrhage that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and abuts the inked margin  The specimen is entirely submitted in K L  with the fibrotic area in K  The smallest piece is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable yellow gold adipose tissue which is entirely submitted in M  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Margaret A Ferrell  M D  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT MEDIAL ASPECT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL ASPECT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  John H Eichhorn  M D  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Tissue Processed CLINICAL DATA  Left breast carcinoma  with positive margins on prior excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING NUMEROUS CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE OR IN SITU CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision  long  lateral  short  superior   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm portion of tan red fibrofatty breast tissue with a short black stitch designating the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  An exposed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic cavity consistent with a previous biopsy site is along the anterior aspect  The cavity has been previously and partially stitched together with black sutures  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a focal bright yellow area consistent with fat necrosis surrounding the hemorrhagic cavity  The cavity focally abuts the medial margin  and comes to 0 9cm of the lateral  1 4cm of the posterior  0 5cm of the inferior  and 2 2cm of the superior margin  The surrounding focally dense gray white fibrous tissue shows cystic change  The clear serous fluid filled cysts average 0 2cm in diameter  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm gray yellow calcification within the dense gray white fibrous tissue  0 9cm from the cavity and 1 4cm from the closest posterior margin in the mid to inferior portion of the specimen  Another cluster of gritty tan yellow calcifications measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  and is located inferior to the first  0 4cm from the closest medial margin  and 1 7cm from the cavity  The remaining fibrous tissue shows focal nodularity with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the cavity to closest margins as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The first calcified focus is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the second as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections along the posterior and posteromedial aspect of the cavity  the region corresponding to the margin of concern in the prior excision  are submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  This case was reviewed again  and at the request of the patient  who is a physician  additional tissue from the specimen was submitted for processing in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A single duct in profile within the biopsy cavity wall on one of the eight additional slides shows residual ductal carcinoma in situ  and this tiny focus is 1 0cm from a blue inked margin  anterior   No stromal or lymphatic invasion is identified in the additional sections  Fibrocystic changes  harboring calcifications  are again noted  Addendum  1 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT  RE  EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 51 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENSIVELY INVOLVING THE ENTIRE SPECIMEN INCLUDING THE MAJORITY OF RESECTION MARGINS  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 20                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal two separated firm white  tan irregular stellate regions extending to inked margins  REMOVED_DATE and 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  Representative sections are frozen as FX 1  Entire specimen submitted in A through J  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY   INVASION CARCINOMA PROBABLY LOBULAR WITH SIGNET RING CELLS  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  09 AUG 95 at 12 00 CLINICAL DATA  36 year old women with calcifications on mammogram and family history of breast cancer  who is undergoing a needle biopsy of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  A SINGLE MICROSOPIC FOCUS   0 1CM   PRESENT LESS THAN 0 1CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MIXED COMEDO AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The single focus of invasive carcinoma consists of a few single malignant cells that infiltrates a microscopic area less than 0 1cm  slide D   The microscopic nature of the invasive component precludes an accurate assessment of tumor grade  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The ductal carcinoma in situ is present in 4 of 11 slides  Dr  Koerner concurs with the diagnosis  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  15 AUG 95 at 16 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through K  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT   NO GROSS EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
