OVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm unoriented lumpectomy specimen containing a needle localization wire  The externally unremarkable tissue is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm spiculated  tan white firm area located 1 0cm from the nearest inked margin  A representative section of this lesion is frozen as FX 3  now resubmitted as cassette D  Representative sections of the remaining tissue are submitted as cassettes E N  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan  rubbery lymph node which is bisected and frozen entirely as FX 4  now resubmitted as cassette O  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast with axillary node dissection  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of attached axillary sampling  A REMOVED_DATE x 10 8cm skin ellipse is attached  with an areola which measures 3 5cm in diameter and a nipple which is inverted and measures 0 6cm in diameter  The skin contains no grossly evident scars or retraction but does contain multiple seborrheic keratoses  The surgical margins are inked blue and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm solid  firm  ill defined white yellow mass which is located at the midline and slightly inferiorly in the breast parenchyma  The mass has a gritty cut surface and extends to within 0 4cm of the deep margin  The tumor is greater than 4 0cm away from the nipple and does not account for the nipple retraction noted  Elsewhere in the breast tissue  away from the tumor mass  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm white  firm  well defined nodule which is greater than 1 0cm from all surgical margins  The remaining parenchyma consists of unremarkable yellow white fibrofatty tissue with no focal lesions  Multiple tan  rubbery lymph nodes are identified within the axillary tail  Section code  P  tumor at closest approach to deep margin Q U  tumor to deep margin V  white nodule  separate from tumor  W  representative section of unremarkable parenchyma X  one lymph node  sectioned Y  one lymph node  bivalved Z  three lymph nodes AA  two lymph nodes BB  two lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm simple mastectomy specimen  which is oriented by a short suture at the superior aspect  and by the previous biopsy site which is towards the lateral portion of the specimen  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x 10 9cm skin ellipse with an areola measuring 3 9cm in diameter and a nipple measuring 2 3cm in diameter  The skin is remarkable for a 3 2cm curvilinear fresh incision located REMOVED_DATE lateral to the nipple  The skin is otherwise unremarkable with no evidence of nipple or skin retraction  The surgical margins are inked blue  and the fresh biopsy cavity is inked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fresh biopsy cavity which extends to within 1 4cm of the deep margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable yellow fibrofatty tissue with no grossly evident focal lesions  The breast tissue is extensively searched for lymph nodes but none is identified  Section code  CC GG  biopsy cavity to nearest deep margin HH  biopsy cavity II  representative section of parenchyma away from biopsy cavity  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1A and 1B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT BREAST AXILLARY LEVEL 1   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE   SENTINEL RIGHT BREAST   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  4  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  LEFT   NEGATIVE FOR