ing assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 25     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right Breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white firm stellate lesion that extends to the inked resection margin  Submitted entirely in A through G  with the suspicious area in C and D  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
