Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 44 CLINICAL DATA  Lesion on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM MAXIMUM DIAMETER IN TISSUE SECTION  EXTENDING TO WITHIN O 2 CM OF A RESECTION MARGIN  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  All of the tumor is invasive  an in situ component is not observed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 33                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 49     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm round  firm white nodule 0 2cm from the closest inked margin  An accompanying specimen X ray shows an irregular opacity  A representative portion is frozen as FX  1  now A  The remainder is submitted in B G with the nodule submitted in B D  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
