Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 31 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma  with positive axillary node  please assess margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE LATERAL ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW NUCLEAR GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN AND 0 1CM FROM THE INFERIOR RESECTION MARGIN 2  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 6 OF 6 LYMPH NODES  3  BREAST   ADDITIONAL AXILLA TISSUE    EXCISION  SPECIMEN NOT RECEIVED BY PATHOLOGY LAB  DR  SMITH HAS BEEN NOTIFIED  4  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  5  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  BENIGN BREAST TISSUE HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast carcinoma   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked superior half in black  the inferior half in blue  and overinked the anterior with green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm white firm stellate area located 0 3cm of the anterior  closest resection margin  in the lateral half of the specimen  A biopsy cavity is present in the medial half  Representative sections of the tumor are submitted in A D and the biopsy cavity in E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a fragment of soft tan adipose tissue measuring 6 x 5 x 1cm with an ellipse of skin measuring 2 x  5cm  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in F through I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional interior margin  right breast  are two fragments of adipose tan soft tissue measuring in aggregate 2 x 2 x  5cm  One fragment contains firm  nodular fibrous area that measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 x  5cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  right breast  is a fragment of tan  fibroadipose tissue measuring 10 x 2 x  5cm  Representative sections are submitted in K through O  Please note that there are additional specimens taken on the yellow sheet called  additional axillary tissue  that was not received  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA GROSSLY NEGATIVE MARGINS  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST   ADDITIONAL AXILLA TISSUE    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN    EXCIS PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION , Unchecked.
