arance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 09 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number   left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm previously blue dyed fibrofatty breast tissue with a localizing wire in place and an accompanying radiograph  There is a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The specimen is black inked medially  blue inked laterally  red inked superiorly  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic cavity with adjacent fat necrosis consistent with a previous biopsy site which abuts the lateral inferior posterior margins and comes to within 0 5cm of the medial superior and 2 0cm from the anterior margins  Probable residual tumors grossly identified  The remaining parenchyma is predominately yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with thin white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially for posterior to anterior as A J  with radial sections of the posterior margin in A and parenchyma toward anterior margin in J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan red rubbery fatty lymph node which is bisected to reveal a tan smooth surface  Specimen is entirely submitted as K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final shave margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which has a short suture designating superior  red inked   and long suture designating the lateral  and a double suture designating surface furthest from tumor  black inked   Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a focally blue dyed yellow lobulated fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial as follows  L  Lateral most margin  M  Full thickness section  N O  Inferior margin  P  Superior margin  Q T  Inferior margin  U  Medial most margin  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  SMN                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL  EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 57 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The largest diameter of the invasive carcinoma as measured on a glass slide is 1 4cm  However  the invasive carcinoma is present in 8 of 12 slides indicating that the carcinoma is present in a significant  approximately 2 3  portion of the biopsy specimen  Thus  the tumor appears to span an area greater than 2 0cm  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT THROUGH ENTIRE TISSUE  INTERMEDIATE AND HIGH GRADE  WITH COMEDO NECROSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  3  THE INTRA OPERATIVE GROSS DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protien  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm segment of fibrofatty breast tissue with localization wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm tan  firm nodular area that extends to within 0 1cm of the inked margin grossly  A second 0 6cm fragment of tan  fibrofatty tissue is present  this is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan yellow unremarkable tissue  The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes A through L  with suspicious area in A  and the second fragment of tissue entirely in L  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  AREA GROSSLY HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
