ing of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 1 705 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm breast specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm axillary tail  The breast specimen contains an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9 9cm nipple containing skin ellipse  The nipple is grossly unremarkable  The skin ellipse contains a 4 6cm well healed scar in the inferior portion of skin ellipse  The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm white  firm  stellate mass deep to the previously noted scar  The stellate mass is 1 4cm from the closest deep resection margin  Other areas within the breast are firm  white  irregular  and contain multiple microcysts ranging from 0 1cm and less in greatest dimension  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow and separated by white fibrous strands and grossly unremarkable  The axillary tail is removed from the main specimen and dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging from 1 6cm to 0 3cm in greatest dimension  White  firm  hard areas are noted in many of the lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  A  closest resection margin  represented by deep resection margin B E  representative sections of the firm stellate mass F H  irregular  white  firm areas not associated with main mass I R  representative sections of lymph nodes  from axillary tail S  representative section of scar on skin ellipse and nipple  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE U