Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 MAY 99 ACCESSIONED ON  28 MAY 99 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA  Re excision from close margin with DCIS                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  ANTERIOR MARGIN   RE EXCISION  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 17 27                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast anterior margin  is an aggregate of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  one of the    contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm skin ellipse with a centrally located linear scar  The specimens are inked and entirely submitted in cassettes B C  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Katharine Treadway  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  ANTERIOR MARGIN   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 43 CLINICAL DATA  Mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO A MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The tumor cells display endocrine features  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue  containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan  well circumscribed nodule that abuts several margins  Representative sections of the nodule are submitted in A through C  representative sections of grossly unremarkable parenchyma are submitted in D and E  Gross Description by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Resident  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  ABUTTING MARGIN  O R  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
