Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 23 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  CARCINOSARCOMA WITH FOCAL CARTILAGINOUS AND OSSEOUS DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is composed of both malignant epithelial and mesenchymal  sarcomatous  areas  These two components are distinct and do not show any merging from the carcinoma into the sarcoma  Immunoperoxidase stains confirm divergent differentiation  with cytokeratins being positive only in the epithelial areas and vimentin and desmin only in the sarcomatous regions  S 100 only stains the carcinoma  Although the differential diagnosis includes a metaplastic carcinoma with extensive sarcomatous areas  there is usually more blending of the epithelial and mesenchymal areas in metaplastic carcinoma  Also  immunoperoxidase usually shows some keratin positivity in the sarcomatous areas in a metaplastic carcinoma  Another interesting feature in this case is that the background of this tumor is reminiscent of a phylloides tumor  with broad stromal fronds focally covered by malignant epithelium  This feature raises the possibility that this tumor is arising in a high grade phylloides  All margins are greater than 0 2cm  No angiolymphatic invasion is seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the case and agrees with this interpretation  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 13 15                                                                                     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     ADDENDUM  ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION   The tumor size is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  see gross description   No lymph nodes were identified in the axillary tail  Sections taken from this region also do not reveal lymph nodes  Added by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  18 MAY 00 at 16 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right modified radical mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm tan wrinkled skin ellipse and a 2 9cm symmetrical nipple areolar complex  A short suture designates superior and long suture designates the axillary tail per the surgeon  There is a 5 5cm well healed curvilinear scar approximately 5 0cm lateral to the areola  The specimen is inked black and serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm well demarcated tan red  focally necrotic mass which comes within 2 7cm of the posterior margin of resection  closest margin  and approximately 0 5cm from the skin  Approximately 1 5cm superior posterior to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm area of skin wedge  The posterior margin is retracted  Sectioning of this area reveals tan white fibrous tissue  A mass cannot grossly be identified in this area  The remaining breast tissue reveals approximately 65  yellow adipose tissue and 35  tan white unremarkable fibrous stroma  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail is present containing no definite lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Tumor  E  Posterior resection margin adjacent to tumor  F  Posterior margin  area of retraction  G  Random breast tissue  H J  Possible lymph nodes from axillary tail  Gross Description by  DELIA FINNIE Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Danielle D Elliott  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Koerner M D   Frederick Carl Reports To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Advanced breast cancer with minimal response to neoadjuvant chemotherapy  suture at 12 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH EXTENSIVE NECROSIS  SEE TABLE  1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 15 OUT OF 15 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Immunoperoxidase stains performed on formalin fixed tissue show the tumor cells stain for cytokeratin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 CAM 5 2  and E cadherin  with focal cytokeratin 7 staining  There are scattered cells which stain for calponin and cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE The cells are negative for cytokeratin 20 and GCDFP 15  This profile is consistent with a primary breast carcinoma  The focal calponin staining suggests myoepithelial differentiation  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  gross measurement  Grade  3  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast  and is a is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 9cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm irregular to elliptical portion of tan skin which displays a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nipple areolar complex  On the posterior aspect there are two metal clips in the upper outer quadrant  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior aspect is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan white lobulated  well circumscribed  indurated and focally hemorrhagic mass in the upper outer quadrant  The mass corresponds to the two metal clips  The mass comes to 1 5cm to the posterior margin  The remaining parenchyma is tan white  yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue and unremarkable  Sectioning through the axillary tail reveals multiple tan pink lymph nodes  which range from 0 2cm to 2 5cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representatives sections of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node trisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node trisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of tumor  with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing additional lymph nodes  Gross Dictation by Tara A Shea  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Less than 10  of tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
